  "subtitle": "This or that: ce livre, cette maison, ces livres. Before a masculine word that starts with a vowel or a mute h, use cet: cet hôtel. French has no separate “near” and “far” word: ce means this and that, and you add -ci or -là to choose. Quel, quelle, quels, quelles mean which or what.",
